// expected: undefined: Undefined
//
// A variadic parameter whose element type cannot be resolved is an error, never
// a `void` parameter. Every DotsType case used to resolve its element and fall
// through to nil, while the `variadic` flag is read from the AST shape
// independently - so the parameter became `void` and callers still built a slice
// for it:
//
//	%t4 = getelementptr inbounds i8, ptr %t3, i32 0   ; GEP of the slice VALUE
//	call void @main.f(void %t3, ptr null)
//
// clang rejects that, and when a scope happened to carry the binding the slice
// construction computed a garbage element size instead and the compiler panicked
// with "alloc: implausible size".
//
// The BARE name is deliberate. The same fixture with a QUALIFIED unresolved name
// (`...fmt.Stringer` in a file that does not import fmt) makes the compiler
// segfault in runtime.memcpy on roughly 2-7% of runs - see the work log,
// round 81 - so this pins the rule without carrying that flake in the suite.
package main

func f(args ...Undefined) {}

func main() {
	f()
}
